                <pb facs="0238" n="972" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg972"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sill to Mr. Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Seoul</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-10-26"><hi rendition="#italic">October 26,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Japanese minister and officers of his legation and army have been sent to Japan.
                    Count Inoye is coming to Seoul as special ambassador. The King is under strict
                    duress. His life in peril. I do not recognize decrees forced from him. Allen’s
                    conduct of affairs excellent.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sill.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
